=== ROUND: README.md ===
$ grep -n 'rabadon on' README.md
32:rabadon on                # arm it — init leaves you in watch mode, this is the line that makes refusals real
133:Propose-and-hold is the law in **every** mode: nothing in rabadon edits your working tree except `rabadon repair --apply`, and a human types that. The text handed to the proposer names **files, never lines** — a line number is a claim about where the bug *is*, and rabadon only knows where the error *surfaced* — and it never forwards the arbiter's raw output on its own. The repair call is the one place rabadon spends tokens, so it is booked on the ledger as a `COST`: characters in and out measured exactly, the token figure labelled as the estimate it is.

--- remove the `rabadon on` line from README.md ---
$ diff README.md /tmp/f1c1.tmp
32d31
< rabadon on                # arm it — init leaves you in watch mode, this is the line that makes refusals real

